**Goal:** `deploy/make-bundle.sh <label>` builds `dist/bundle-<label>.tar.gz` (0600) with everything a server needs;

```json:metadata
{"files": ["docs/11-deployment.md", "otter-server/deploy/lib.sh"], "verifyCommand": "`cd otter-server && for f in deploy/*.sh deploy/bundle/*.sh deploy/test/*.sh; do bash -n \"$f\" || exit 1; done && deploy/test/bundle_test.sh`", "acceptanceCriteria": ["`make-bundle.sh fi-1 [VERSION]` (default: newest version in `dist/` by `sort -V`) creates `dist/bundle-fi-1.tar.gz` (mode 0600) containing `bundle-fi-1/` with: `otter-node-amd64`, `otter-node-arm64`, `node.key`, `tls.crt`, `tls.key` (the staged pair if present), `manifest.bin`, `node.toml`, `probe.env`, `otter-node.service`, `otter-backup.{service,timer}`, `site/index.html`, `invites/*.bin` (every pending bootstrap invite), the four scripts, `SHA256SUMS`; and writes `dist/bundle-fi-1.invites` listing the included invite files.", "It refuses to run when `manifest.bin` doesn't list the node or its pins don't include the bundle certificate's pin (message: run `manifest sign`).", "`deploy/test/bundle_test.sh` (no root, no VM) builds a bundle from a throwaway admin dir, verifies `SHA256SUMS`, rewrites `/etc/otter` and `/var/lib/otter` paths to temp dirs and passes `otter-node check`, and greps the unit for `ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/otter-node run --config /etc/otter/node.toml`.", "Scripts start with `set -euo pipefail`, print every action (`==> …`), and `bash -n` passes for all of them.", "The decoy page has no Otter/OtterMSG wording."]}
```

**Goal:** the app can change its display name offline-first and publishes a new signed directory entry when online;

```json:metadata
{"files": ["otter-android/core/proto"], "verifyCommand": "`cd otter-android && JAVA_HOME=~/.gradle/jdks/eclipse_adoptium-21-amd64-linux.2 ./gradlew :core:data:testDebugUnitTest --tests '*Profile*' --tests '*DirectorySync*' --tests '*Registration*'`", "acceptanceCriteria": ["`ProfileRepository.setDisplayName(raw)`: trims; 1–64 code points else `ProfileError.Empty/TooLong`; stores the name in `account` and sets `profile_pending` in one transaction; `AccountRepository.account` emits the new name at once.", "While a session is up, a pending name is published as entry `version = entryVersion + 1` with the same username, keys, `identity_sig`, `can_invite = true` and `registered_ms = account.createdMs`; on OK the pending flag clears and `entryVersion` is stored. `CONFLICT` → reads its own entry from `directory()`, continues from that version (max 3 tries). Network errors leave it pending and retry on the next session or after 30 s.", "`DirectorySync` sees its own entry: raises `entryVersion` to the entry's version; when nothing is pending and the name differs, adopts it (restore/second install cases).", "Registration builds the entry through `DirectoryEntries` and sets `registered_ms`.", "Tests (`FakeNode`): offline edit → online publishes once; a second client sees the new contact name and the direct chat title; conflict path; validation; pending survives an app restart (new graph on the same DB)."]}
```
